        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "New capacity is roughly 2x the old one. CPython really grows by about 1.125x plus a constant."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "3. Why append() is Amortized O(1)",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Usually a free slot exists — O(1)",
            "Now and then a resize copies all — O(n)",
            "Those costly resizes are rare",
            "Average cost per append stays O(1)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "lst.pop()       # O(1), no shift",
            "lst.pop(0)      # O(n), shifts all",
            "lst.insert(0,x) # O(n)"
          ],
          "note": "only the END is cheap"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "sticky",
          "title": "Need the Front?",
          "text": "Working at the front of a list shifts every item. Use `collections.deque` — `popleft()` is ==O(1)==."
        }
      ]
    },
